; RUN: llc -mtriple=bpfel -mcpu=v3 < %s | FileCheck %s
;
; MachineLICM hoists the address of a global array out of the loop. In a loop
; without calls, the loop body uses a copy of the hoisted address, not a new
; LD_imm64. In a loop with a call, the address is rematerialized in the loop.
;
; many_arrays reads more global arrays than there are registers. MachineLICM
; hoists all twelve addresses. The register allocator keeps as many as it can
; in registers and rematerializes the others with LD_imm64 in the loop. It
; does not spill an address to the stack.

@buf = global [1024 x i8] zeroinitializer, align 1
